  "major": "International Studies",
  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for International Studies (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 15+15+16+15+15+14+15+15 = 120 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 120). The program is a Bachelor of Arts (standard for AIC humanities/social science programs; the plan does not print a degree abbreviation). Twelve credits of foreign language are required: Introductory I & II (Freshman year), Intermediate III & IV (Sophomore year). The Language Note states the language sequence start may be moved to second or third year. Specialization Area Courses #1-4 (12 credits) are four courses in ONE specialization area: International Security (CRJ1400, CRJ3331, CRJ3641, CYS1000, CYS2000, CYS2500); International Economy (IBS1400, IBS3400, IBS3410, IBS3820, IBS4430, POL3412); or Global Health and Environment (PCH1030, PCH2030, PCH3250, PCH3630, BIO1130, SOC3440). The INS Elective (Sophomore Fall) is one of IBS1420 Diverse Cultures of the World, INT2100 Power Identity and Privilege, or PHI2010 World Religion. Senior Spring capstone: INS4800 International Studies Seminar OR INS4899 International Studies Internship. POL1500 is Comparative Politics (printed as 'POL1 5 00'). General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
